  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The centre of a circle is located at $(2,1)$. The line $x+y=4$ is tangent to the circle. Find the coordinates of the point $P$ where the circle and line meet.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$P\\left(\\frac52,\\frac32\\right)$.\n\nIntersect the tangent with the perpendicular through the centre.",
      "worked": "The radius to $P$ is perpendicular to the tangent. The tangent has gradient $-1$, so the radius has gradient $1$. Through $(2,1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=x-2\\\\y&=x-1.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $x+y=4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+(x-1)&=4\\\\2x&=5\\\\x&=\\frac52\\\\y&=\\frac52-1\\\\y&=\\frac32.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $P\\left(\\frac52,\\frac32\\right)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 96
  },
